IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), piece cb2 (Parts VII to X) -- THE NOUNS.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE IS. Only the nouns that two or more cb2 modules need: the three forms of a security,
-- the two kinds of endorsement, the ways of taking an interest in a security, and the three kinds of
-- appointee under Part IX. It holds no rule. Every type is declared here once; the rule modules import it.
-- Every enumeration constructor is a specific phrase, because after the merge the names of all the
-- pieces of the Act sit in one folder and a name defined twice cannot be used at all.

§ `The nouns of Parts VII to X`

§§ `The forms of a security -- s 48(3) to (6)`

-- The Act says a security is "in registered form", "in order form" or "in bearer form" and defines each
-- in its own subsection (s 48(4), (5), (6)); the three are the answers a person can give when asked what
-- form a security takes. A fourth constructor answers that it is none of the three.
-- src:728 | Registered form
-- src:729 | (4) A security is in registered form if
-- src:730 | (a) it specifies a person entitled to the security or to the rights it evidences, and its transfer is capable of being recorded in a securities register; or
-- src:731 | (b) it bears a statement that it is in registered form.
-- src:732 | Order form
-- src:733 | (5) A debt obligation is in order form where, by its terms, it is payable to the order or assigns of any person therein specified with reasonable certainty or to that person’s order.
-- src:734 | Bearer form
-- src:735 | (6) A security is in bearer form if it is payable to bearer according to its terms and not by reason of any endorsement.
@ref CBCA s 48(4) to (6) registered form, order form, bearer form (src:728-735)
DECLARE `Form of a security` IS ONE OF
    `a security in registered form`
    `a security in order form`
    `a security in bearer form`
    `a security in none of the three forms in section 48`

§§ `Kinds of endorsement -- s 65(4)`

-- src:946 | Special or blank
-- src:947 | (4) An endorsement may be special or in blank.
@ref CBCA s 65(4) special or blank (src:946-947)
DECLARE `Kind of endorsement` IS ONE OF
    `an endorsement in blank`
    `a special endorsement`

§§ `Ways of taking an interest in a security -- s 48(2) "purchaser"`

-- "Purchaser means a person who takes an interest or right in a security by sale, mortgage, hypothec,
-- pledge, issue, reissue, gift or any other voluntary transaction". The last constructor answers that
-- the interest was taken in a way that is not a voluntary transaction (by operation of law, say).
-- src:716 | purchaser means a person who takes an interest or right in a security by sale, mortgage, hypothec, pledge, issue, reissue, gift or any other voluntary transaction; (acquéreur)
@ref CBCA s 48(2) purchaser (src:716)
DECLARE `Way of taking an interest in a security` IS ONE OF
    `taking an interest in a security by sale`
    `taking an interest in a security by mortgage`
    `taking an interest in a security by hypothec`
    `taking an interest in a security by pledge`
    `taking an interest in a security by issue`
    `taking an interest in a security by reissue`
    `taking an interest in a security by gift`
    `taking an interest in a security by another voluntary transaction`
    `taking an interest in a security in a way that is not a voluntary transaction`

§§ `The three kinds of appointee under Part IX`

-- Part IX speaks of "a receiver, receiver-manager or sequestrator" and gives each a different function
-- (ss 94 and 95). The core's Party has only `a receiver or receiver-manager`.
-- src:1168 | PART IX Receivers, Receiver-managers and Sequestrators
@ref CBCA Part IX Receivers, Receiver-managers and Sequestrators (src:1168)
DECLARE `Kind of appointee under Part IX` IS ONE OF
    `a receiver appointed in respect of property of a corporation`
    `a receiver-manager of a corporation`
    `a sequestrator of property of a corporation`
